      "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #47801\n\nOn ROCm 7.2.1 with RDNA3 GPUs (gfx1100), `F.scaled_dot_product_attention` uses the math backend when `head_dim > 256`. This backend is not run-to-run deterministic at sequence length 4096 (1024x1024 images), causing VAE decode to produce slightly different outputs for identical inputs.\n\nThis fix wraps the SDPA call with `torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True, warn_only=True)` when on ROCm and `head_dim > 256`, ensuring bitwise reproducible outputs while maintaining performance for other configurations.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Modified `QwenImage21AttentionBlock.forward()` in `python/sglang/multimodal_gen/runtime/models/vaes/autoencoder_kl_qwenimage21.py`\n- Added ROCm detection and conditional deterministic algorithm flag\n- Preserves and restores the previous deterministic algorithm state\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Verified fix logic with unit tests on CPU\n- [x] Confirmed deterministic outputs with repeated calls\n- [ ] Test on ROCm 7.2.1 with gfx1100 GPU (requires hardware)\n- [ ] Verify no performance regression on CUDA GPUs\n- [ ] Run existing Qwen-Image 2.1 test suite\n\n🤖 Generated with [QoderWork](https://qoder.com)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41376950395](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41376950395)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41376950298](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41376950298)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41376950401](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41376950401)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
