            "body": "Ran this change end to end on RDNA3 (gfx1100, W7900-class), single GPU. Setup: the `rocm/pytorch` ROCm 7.2.1 image (`torch 2.9.1+rocm7.2.1.lw.gitff65f5bc`), a downstream build of SGLang with the diff of dada15c applied to `autoencoder_kl_qwenimage21.py`, `--attention-backend torch_sdpa`. All renders used the same prompt, 30 steps and one server. The change was switched off for the first two renders and on for the rest. Hashes are the sha256 of the decoded RGB pixels.\n\n| render | change | pixels sha256 | wall time |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1024x1024, seed 1015, #1 | off | `cfda7f55...` | 49.60 s |\n| 1024x1024, seed 1015, #2 | off | `ebf349dd...` | 49.60 s |\n| 1024x1024, seed 1015, #3 | on | `b5616197...` | 49.61 s |\n| 1024x1024, seed 1015, #4 | on | `b5616197...` | 49.72 s |\n| 1344x768, seed 1000 | on | `5c64752a...` | 48.74 s |\n\n- With the change on, the two 1024x1024 renders are identical; with it off they differ, as in #47801.\n- The 1344x768 hash matches an earlier run without the change (head_dim is above 256 there too, so the flag is on for that call, and the output is unchanged).\n- Time: no measurable difference (+0.01 s / +0.12 s against one render without the change; single renders, so within run-to-run noise).\n",
